Z||000000||x-thumpr-x||12-31-2001||02:09 PM||||Well I took it in this morning and it failed the safety.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Lets see. it failed becuase:<P>  Missing a rear reflector  <BR>  Driver sail panel broken<BR>  Front plate holder broken (corner)<BR>  Missing Power window switch<BR>  Front rotors too thin. came in at 9.1<BR>  should be no lower then 9.68 <BR>  E-brake lever sticking.<BR>  lower rad support rusted out<BR>  tire had "A" crack<BR>  No tire jack in car.<P>O.K.  I'll give them credit for the Rad support, & rotors. I can put another tire on the car (2 spair sets) But the rest! what a joke.  I asked to see the safety book, service rep went to see his boss. They dropped the sail panel and plate holder form the safety.  I said what-ever, I'll just take the parts off the parts car. Rotors on the car are almost brand new. And the caliper will be romoved and greased up and (and cable) so they don't stick. (sticks 1-5 tries on the e-brake) Not sure yet on how the rad support is in the spare though.<BR>looks like another days works, when all done, bring car back to shop. They just look over what needed to be done the pass the car. (hopefully!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
